    "question": {
      ":question/id": "8c9dd031-3a09-5691-8158-a73a0ebc9767",
      ":question/problem": "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{1 - \\left(y + 3\\right)^{2}}$ for $\\,|\\left(y+3\\right)|<1.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\sqrt{1 - \\left(y + 3\\right)^{2}} \\\\ (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - \\left(y + 3\\right)^{2}}})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - \\left(y + 3\\right)^{2}}})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - \\left(y + 3\\right)^{2}}})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\cancel{\\text{d}x}}\\,\\cancel{\\text{d}x} & =\\int (1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - \\left(y + 3\\right)^{2}}})\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\arcsin{\\left(y + 3 \\right)} & =x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n\\arcsin{\\left(y + 3 \\right)}=x+C.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
